{title: Walk in Newness of Life}
{subtitle: Romans 6:4}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bbmaj7] | [Bbmaj7] | [Gm7] | [Cm7] |
| [F7sus4] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bbmaj7]What shall we say about [Gm7]grace
Should we keep on [Cm7]sinning more
[Bbmaj7]By no means we died to [Gm7]sin
So how can we [Cm7]live in it
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bbmaj7]Do you not know the [Gm7]truth
We were baptized [Cm7]into Christ
[Bbmaj7]Into His death we [Gm7]went
All of us who [Cm7]followed
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bbmaj7]Buried with Him into [Gm7]death
In order that [Cm7]we might rise
As [Bbmaj7]Christ was raised from the [Gm7]dead
We too walk [Cm7]in newness
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bbmaj7]United in His death
[Gm7]We will be united in [Cm7]life
[Bbmaj7]Our old self was cru[Gm7]cified
The bo[Cm7]dy of sin is gone
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Ebmaj7]No longer slaves to [Dm7]sin
Rendered [Gm7]powerless is the bo[Cm7]dy
[Ebmaj7]We have died and are set [Dm7]free
[Cm7]Free from the old life [Bbmaj7]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Gm7]Walk in new[Cm7]ness of life [Bbmaj7]
[Gm7]Raised by the glory of the [Cm7]Father
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
